# Scripts run on Linux. A CRLF here breaks them on the box.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Same for the files that go to /etc or /opt on the box: systemd units and
# drop-ins, sysctl, Caddy. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows, `git archive`
# exported them with CRLF (measured 10.11.2026: 6 to 40 CR bytes per file).
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.caddy text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
*.tpl text eol=lf
